<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n104603" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τράφηξ</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ᾰ]</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ηκος</span>, ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>beam</i> in framework of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑλέπολις,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Bito
				53.4
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>spear,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Lyc.
				1001
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>baker's board,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				EM
				764.35
			</span></i>:—so perh. in <i><span class="en">
				Lyc.
				641
			</span></i> (unless the sense is more general, v. Sch.).
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b>
			<i>handle of an oar,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>
			
				s.v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρόπηκος;</span>
			 or <i>gunwale</i> on which the rowlocks are fixed, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				22.1604.40
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iv B. C.)</span>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>EM</u>
				764.36
			</span></i>.—<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τράφηξ</span> seems to
			be the true form; but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τράπηξ, τρόπηξ,
				τροφῆς</span> are found in cod. of <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
</div>